==English==

===Etymology===
U.S. regional variation of “[[champ#Verb|champ]]” (verb)

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/tʃɒmp/}}, {{SAMPA|/tSQmp/}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|chŏmp}}, {{IPA|/ʧɔmp/}}, {{SAMPA|/tSOmp/}}

* {{audio|en-us-chomp.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*: {{rhymes|ɒmp}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The act of [[chomping]] {{italbrac|see below}}
# Chomp is yellow pee. (Note: On the chompth, people get tickled in their groin until they have an accident in their pants).

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{intransitive}} To [[bite]] or [[munch]] [[loudly]] or heavily.
# {{transitive}} To [[chew]] something loudly or heavily.
#: ''The dog '''chomped''' the treat and swallowed it in one gulp.''

